# The image is built from this directory (context ./switchboard — CI, the release
# workflow and the Supervisor all build from here), and `COPY rootfs /` would
# otherwise bake in whatever the developer's machine left lying around. A stale
# .pyc is not inert: Python will import a bytecode file whose .py source has been
# renamed or deleted if it lands in a directory on sys.path, so a rename that
# looks complete in git can be silently undone inside the container. Since
# v0.108.0 the AppArmor profile write-locks /usr and the AGI tree, so a stale
# cache baked in here could not even be replaced at runtime.
#
# Until v0.108.0 this file sat at the repository root, outside the build
# context, where no build ever read it.
**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]
**/.pytest_cache/
**/.DS_Store
